1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:01,362
One falling
apple sparked

2
00:00:01,375 --> 00:00:02,425
the wildest question—

3
00:00:02,562 --> 00:00:03,800
does the Moon
fall too?

4
00:00:04,330 --> 00:00:05,434
Impossible, Newton!

5
00:00:05,573 --> 00:00:06,712
What holds
the Moon up?

6
00:00:06,978 --> 00:00:07,738
Invisible gravity—

7
00:00:07,865 --> 00:00:09,414
every mass pulls
every other mass!

8
00:00:09,630 --> 00:00:11,243
Next, Newton
shot sunlight

9
00:00:11,256 --> 00:00:12,293
through a glass prism—

10
00:00:12,343 --> 00:00:13,331
splitting white light

11
00:00:13,343 --> 00:00:14,857
into seven
rainbow colors!

12
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:16,758
Every action
triggers an equal,

13
00:00:16,836 --> 00:00:17,738
opposite reaction—

14
00:00:18,030 --> 00:00:19,211
Whoa! That steel ball

15
00:00:19,222 --> 00:00:20,352
nearly knocked me over!

16
00:00:20,630 --> 00:00:22,217
Gravity bends
a fall into orbit—

17
00:00:22,254 --> 00:00:23,454
uniting falling apples

18
00:00:23,467 --> 00:00:24,715
and moons
under one law!

19
00:00:25,330 --> 00:00:27,288
Rockets, satellites,
Moon landings today—

20
00:00:27,444 --> 00:00:29,546
every launch flies
on Isaac Newton's laws.
